From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:27:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Input: ft3658 - name the Google driver the protocol follows

The header says the protocol follows Google's GPL FocalTech driver for
Pixel devices. Name the repository, the directory, the branch and the
files, so a reviewer can follow it to the source: focaltech_spi.c for
the framing, the status check, the 64-byte alignment rule and the CS-high
delay, and focaltech_core.c for the power sequence and the report.

Suggested-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c
index 17bdeb15c..4309c8664 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c
@@ -3,7 +3,10 @@
  * FocalTech FT3658 touchscreen driver (SPI)
  *
  * The FT3658 is the touch controller of the Google Pixel 7. The protocol
- * follows Google's GPL FocalTech driver for Pixel devices:
+ * follows Google's GPL FocalTech driver for Pixel devices
+ * (kernel/google-modules/touch/focaltech_touch, ft3658/, branch
+ * android-gs-pantah-6.1-android16: focaltech_spi.c for the framing,
+ * focaltech_core.c for the power sequence and the report):
  *   Copyright (c) 2012-2020, FocalTech Systems, Ltd.
  *
  * The controller runs its own firmware from flash; this driver only powers
